course: dictionary
lesson: 6329
title: A motorway is a fast road
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A motorway is a wide, fast road with several lanes going in each direction, made for long journeys by car and lorry. Read the words around it, which are its context: «On a motorway, after a breakdown everyone gets out and waits behind the barrier, away from the traffic.» The traffic here means cars and lorries, so a motorway is a road for vehicles.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Families drive on the motorway for long trips» still makes sense if a motorway is a fast road for long journeys, so the meaning fits.
explain: Different places use different names for the same kind of road. In the UK, Ireland and New Zealand it is a motorway. In the US people say freeway or highway, and in Australia it can be a freeway or a motorway.
explain: Motorways are for cars and lorries, not people on foot or bicycles. Never walk, cycle or play on a motorway. If a car breaks down, everyone gets out on the side away from the traffic and waits behind the barrier.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A motorway has several lanes in each direction, so many vehicles can travel fast in both directions at once.
fact: In the UK, the speed limit on motorways is usually 70 mph.
fact: Motorway services are places beside the road where drivers can stop, rest and fill up with petrol.
fact: The hard shoulder is the strip at the edge of a motorway, used only for emergencies.
exercise: «On a motorway, after a breakdown everyone gets out and waits behind the barrier, away from the traffic.» Where should people wait? | *Behind the barrier, away from the traffic | In the middle of the lane | Under the nearest bridge | On the road, so drivers can see them
exercise: Which of these is a motorway? | A narrow path through the woods for walkers | A small village street with houses on both sides | *A wide, fast road with several lanes each way, for cars and lorries | A lane only for bicycles
exercise: In the UK, what is the usual speed limit on a motorway? | 5 mph | 100 mph on every road | 30 mph | *70 mph
test: Dad's car breaks down on the motorway. What should everyone do? | Stay in the car with the doors open | *Get out on the side away from the traffic and wait behind the barrier | Walk along the lane to find help | Run across to the other side of the road
test: An American asks what a motorway is called in the USA. What is the best answer? | *Freeway or highway | Verge | Motorway | Lorry
exam: Why must you never walk, cycle or play on a motorway? | Because the road is too short to cross | Because the barrier stops you from getting home | *Because the fast traffic is very dangerous | Because motorways are made of soft mud
